WEBVTT

00:00:10.190 --> 00:00:12.360
We lost because of me?

00:00:12.360 --> 00:00:13.580
You kidding me?

00:00:13.580 --> 00:00:16.390
You didn't do anything today either!

00:00:16.390 --> 00:00:18.800
Yeah, I didn't make an error like you.

00:00:18.800 --> 00:00:21.610
You haven't had a hit for several games now.

00:00:21.610 --> 00:00:24.080
Are you a spy from some other team?

00:00:24.080 --> 00:00:25.250
What was that?

00:00:25.250 --> 00:00:26.810
You can't hit or field!

00:00:26.810 --> 00:00:29.300
You're just a good-for-nothing on this team!

00:00:29.300 --> 00:00:32.170
Why don't you stop talking big and practice a little?

00:00:32.170 --> 00:00:34.680
You're just luggage to the Hornets.

00:00:35.330 --> 00:00:36.890
Now you've said it.

00:00:36.890 --> 00:00:38.720
Go to hell!

00:00:38.720 --> 00:00:39.970
Hey, stop, you two!

00:00:39.970 --> 00:00:41.810
Man, shut up.

00:00:41.810 --> 00:00:45.190
Neither of you guys did anything,

00:00:45.190 --> 00:00:47.310
yet you're fighting about the game?

00:00:47.310 --> 00:00:48.970
What are you saying?

00:00:48.970 --> 00:00:53.100
We lost today because of your selfish plays!

00:00:53.100 --> 00:00:54.610
What was that?

00:00:54.610 --> 00:00:56.820
You have no right to say anything!

00:00:56.820 --> 00:00:59.500
Same goes for you!

00:00:59.500 --> 00:01:01.910
You pick a fight over everything you don't like!

00:01:01.910 --> 00:01:03.310
Hey, stop!

00:01:03.310 --> 00:01:05.360
That's because your plays are nothing but jokes!

00:01:05.360 --> 00:01:06.420
That's enough!

00:01:07.810 --> 00:01:12.100
You're all just blindly blaming someone else.

00:01:12.100 --> 00:01:14.270
Hearing you argue makes me sick.

00:01:14.650 --> 00:01:16.840
It's not one person's fault we lost.

00:01:17.610 --> 00:01:23.880
Why don't you reflect on your own plays before you force your sins on someone else?

00:01:30.310 --> 00:01:34.030
How I'll hold the team together, huh?

00:01:35.610 --> 00:01:40.860
egaita yume to koko ni aru ima

00:01:35.610 --> 00:01:40.860
I look at my dream and my current reality,

00:01:40.860 --> 00:01:46.160
futatsu no keshiki mikurabete mo

00:01:40.860 --> 00:01:46.160
but no matter how much I compare the two,

00:01:46.160 --> 00:01:51.540
katachi wo kaete koko ni aru no wa

00:01:46.160 --> 00:01:51.540
the only thing I truly have

00:01:51.540 --> 00:01:56.830
tashika na hitotsuno mono

00:01:51.540 --> 00:01:56.830
is the one and only thing I'm sure of.

00:01:56.830 --> 00:02:02.170
sugiyuku haru wo oshiminagara mo

00:01:56.830 --> 00:02:02.170
Even as I bid a sad farewell to spring,

00:02:02.170 --> 00:02:07.430
bokura no maku aketa ano natsu

00:02:02.170 --> 00:02:07.430
the season of the coming summer began.

00:02:07.430 --> 00:02:12.810
ironna koto wo wakari hajimeta

00:02:07.430 --> 00:02:12.810
I had begun to understand many things

00:02:12.810 --> 00:02:18.900
aki to nanika ushinatta fuyu

00:02:12.810 --> 00:02:18.900
by the fall, but I lost something in the winter.

00:02:18.900 --> 00:02:24.450
garakuta no yama kara

00:02:18.900 --> 00:02:24.450
In the junk I've piled up,

00:02:24.450 --> 00:02:28.530
sagasu ano hi no yume

00:02:24.450 --> 00:02:28.530
I search for the dream I had way back when.

00:02:28.530 --> 00:02:33.830
hibike kono koe yo

00:02:28.530 --> 00:02:33.830
Let my voice echo on.

00:02:33.830 --> 00:02:40.090
hibike kono kokoro yo

00:02:33.830 --> 00:02:40.090
Let my heart resonate.

00:02:40.090 --> 00:02:45.760
namida kareru made

00:02:40.090 --> 00:02:45.760
Until my tears dry up,

00:02:45.760 --> 00:02:50.810
mada denu kotae oitsuzukete

00:02:45.760 --> 00:02:50.810
I'll chase the answer I've been searching for.

00:02:50.810 --> 00:02:56.140
namida hareru made

00:02:50.810 --> 00:02:56.140
Until my tears clear away,

00:02:56.140 --> 00:03:01.150
waga yukue mayoi nagara mo

00:02:56.140 --> 00:03:01.150
though I may lose my way,

00:03:01.150 --> 00:03:04.990
egakikake no ima

00:03:01.150 --> 00:03:04.990
I'll continue to paint the present,

00:03:04.990 --> 00:03:06.490
kizamu

00:03:04.990 --> 00:03:12.240
and carve my existence with my own two hands.

00:03:06.490 --> 00:03:07.780
akashi

00:03:07.780 --> 00:03:12.240
kono te de

00:03:20.030 --> 00:03:21.800
Oh, no! He hit a fly!

00:03:21.800 --> 00:03:23.550
That's the end!

00:03:25.330 --> 00:03:26.890
Game over!

00:03:26.890 --> 00:03:29.270
The Hornets line-up is silenced yet again!

00:03:29.990 --> 00:03:31.530
This gives the Hornets a second—

00:03:37.890 --> 00:03:38.880
Man!

00:03:38.880 --> 00:03:41.110
What the hell's wrong with the Hornets this year?

00:03:41.540 --> 00:03:43.830
They start out losing every game,

00:03:43.830 --> 00:03:45.920
then they start to win, like God's helping them.

00:03:45.920 --> 00:03:47.610
Then just when I think they're going all the way,

00:03:47.610 --> 00:03:49.960
they start yet another series of losses.

00:03:49.960 --> 00:03:52.790
I feel like I'm riding a roller coaster.

00:03:54.070 --> 00:03:56.380
But... they'll win tomorrow!

00:03:57.320 --> 00:03:59.120
After all...

00:03:59.120 --> 00:04:01.380
Shigeno's starting tomorrow.

00:04:02.430 --> 00:04:07.430
A Resolute Will

00:04:02.430 --> 00:04:07.430
A Resolute Will

00:04:09.830 --> 00:04:10.850
Give me a break!

00:04:11.270 --> 00:04:13.770
How many times do you need to lose?

00:04:13.770 --> 00:04:16.760
If we fall out of the running for the top spot,

00:04:16.760 --> 00:04:20.850
we're going to lose our whole audience when we've only just started attracting crowds!

00:04:20.850 --> 00:04:24.860
Are you planning to ruin this opportunity for profit?!

00:04:24.860 --> 00:04:26.130
Goodness...

00:04:28.290 --> 00:04:31.620
Please, have a little more faith in the players.

00:04:32.910 --> 00:04:34.710
Wh-What?!

00:04:34.710 --> 00:04:38.600
Our team this year has enough talent to aim for the championship title.

00:04:39.040 --> 00:04:41.080
Of course they're aiming for the title!

00:04:41.080 --> 00:04:43.710
But talent alone doesn't mean anything!

00:04:43.710 --> 00:04:45.380
Besides, business is all about—

00:04:45.380 --> 00:04:48.820
I have a meeting scheduled with the other coaches right now.

00:04:48.820 --> 00:04:50.060
Please excuse me.

00:04:50.060 --> 00:04:51.090
Y—

00:04:57.230 --> 00:05:00.240
If you can't win the title, you're fired, Stacy!

00:05:03.070 --> 00:05:06.990
Those two consecutive losses cost us, but we can still catch up.

00:05:07.640 --> 00:05:10.910
If we don't stand our ground now, our season's over.

00:05:13.620 --> 00:05:16.390
I'll need to get some good hits today.

00:05:26.240 --> 00:05:28.470
I triggered the losses in the first place.

00:05:28.470 --> 00:05:31.220
We have to win today, no matter what.

00:05:33.500 --> 00:05:34.260
So...

00:05:36.590 --> 00:05:37.630
What do you think?

00:05:40.870 --> 00:05:44.970
For better or for worse, we have a team fueled by emotions.

00:05:44.970 --> 00:05:49.740
If we capitalize on an opportunity, we all get a boost and start a winning streak.

00:05:50.360 --> 00:05:57.160
However, if we fail even once, we sink deep into a slump.

00:05:58.580 --> 00:05:59.580
Yeah.

00:06:00.800 --> 00:06:02.000
As for our tendencies...

00:06:02.840 --> 00:06:05.090
We're not exactly strong in tight games.

00:06:05.640 --> 00:06:09.470
We're even worse when an opponent gets an early lead.

00:06:11.680 --> 00:06:16.980
As it is, we're lacking the manpower to squeeze out victories in tight games.

00:06:18.820 --> 00:06:22.500
So the team is like a pack of wild horses.

00:06:23.710 --> 00:06:27.310
Unless someone puts reins on them and leads,

00:06:27.310 --> 00:06:30.150
we won't ever have true strength as a team.

00:06:32.030 --> 00:06:37.740
Someone who can calmly evaluate situations and control the team.

00:06:39.180 --> 00:06:40.920
Did something happen?

00:06:42.370 --> 00:06:44.160
No, not at all.

00:06:45.970 --> 00:06:50.030
Today, the Hornets play the Browns who are here to get their fourth consecutive win.

00:06:50.950 --> 00:06:55.100
With a duty to revive his ailing Hornets,

00:06:56.300 --> 00:07:00.580
Goro Shigeno, a young southpaw from Japan, steps on to the mound.

00:07:00.580 --> 00:07:04.870
On the other side, the Browns are bringing out their ace who won sixteen games last year

00:07:04.870 --> 00:07:08.360
and pitched for the Korean World Cup team.

00:07:08.360 --> 00:07:11.530
It's the Korean Rocket, Ahn Cheng-Gong.

00:07:11.980 --> 00:07:13.910
Play ball!

00:07:19.450 --> 00:07:20.660
Strike!

00:07:20.660 --> 00:07:21.760
All right.

00:07:21.760 --> 00:07:25.840
Let's end this quickly, and put a spark back into the team.

00:07:26.800 --> 00:07:28.390
Strike!

00:07:28.390 --> 00:07:30.720
That's the way, Shigeno!

00:07:30.720 --> 00:07:32.220
This game is ours!

00:07:32.220 --> 00:07:33.760
Three for three!

00:07:34.720 --> 00:07:36.110
All right!

00:07:36.110 --> 00:07:37.470
Ball!

00:07:49.400 --> 00:07:50.360
Good!

00:07:50.360 --> 00:07:51.280
That was a nice forkball.

00:07:51.280 --> 00:07:52.450
Ball!

00:07:52.450 --> 00:07:54.070
Wh-What?

00:07:54.490 --> 00:07:56.480
Hey, that was a swing!

00:07:56.480 --> 00:07:58.870
Can you check with the third base umpire?

00:07:59.480 --> 00:08:01.670
Why won't you check?

00:08:02.960 --> 00:08:05.650
I judged that he didn't swing.

00:08:05.650 --> 00:08:07.400
We don't need to check with anyone.

00:08:07.400 --> 00:08:09.590
You're free to go talk to him,

00:08:10.190 --> 00:08:12.350
but I have no obligation to argue.

00:08:17.690 --> 00:08:18.790
Damn.

00:08:18.790 --> 00:08:20.860
We got one annoying umpire today.

00:08:24.980 --> 00:08:26.110
Ball.

00:08:26.110 --> 00:08:28.520
That was a strike!

00:08:29.600 --> 00:08:30.540
Ball!

00:08:30.540 --> 00:08:31.930
Ball four!

00:08:31.930 --> 00:08:33.470
Damn it!

00:08:33.470 --> 00:08:33.900
Time out.

00:08:35.220 --> 00:08:37.950
Hey, what's up with that umpire?

00:08:37.950 --> 00:08:40.320
We got an especially tough one today.

00:08:40.320 --> 00:08:43.380
Seeing his calls for the last two low, outside pitches,

00:08:43.380 --> 00:08:45.420
he'll never call those strikes.

00:08:45.420 --> 00:08:46.170
Damn.

00:08:46.170 --> 00:08:48.670
Anyone can tell it's a strike, for God's sake.

00:08:49.540 --> 00:08:51.930
It's nothing. Don't get so upset.

00:08:51.930 --> 00:08:53.710
Your pitches are sharp.

00:08:53.710 --> 00:08:56.300
You can play it safer with your pitches, so let's pitch to contact.

00:08:57.490 --> 00:08:58.640
Sure.

00:08:58.640 --> 00:09:01.140
That umpire's pretty strict today.

00:09:01.140 --> 00:09:03.170
Yeah, that's Mitchell.

00:09:03.170 --> 00:09:08.470
He has a smaller strike zone than most umpires, so not many pitchers like him.

00:09:09.060 --> 00:09:13.150
Shigeno is lucky to have gone this long without meeting him.

00:09:13.150 --> 00:09:16.710
There's already enough pressure on him pitching a game he can't lose...

00:09:16.710 --> 00:09:20.450
It's going to be a tough game for Shigeno.

00:09:21.290 --> 00:09:22.300
Ball!

00:09:22.300 --> 00:09:23.360
Ball four!

00:09:25.070 --> 00:09:26.040
Again?

00:09:27.720 --> 00:09:29.070
Calm down, Shigeno.

00:09:30.080 --> 00:09:31.380
Loosen up.

00:09:38.960 --> 00:09:39.720
Out!

00:09:40.560 --> 00:09:42.390
You're not getting the first run!

00:09:42.960 --> 00:09:43.600
Got it!

00:09:48.110 --> 00:09:48.440
Safe!

00:09:50.500 --> 00:09:51.900
Safe!

00:09:53.860 --> 00:09:56.230
D-Damn.

00:09:57.560 --> 00:09:59.700
We lost the first run again.

00:10:01.370 --> 00:10:03.080
Damn, I really screwed up.

00:10:03.080 --> 00:10:05.040
Man, you suck.

00:10:06.610 --> 00:10:07.950
This is bad.

00:10:07.950 --> 00:10:10.460
It's starting to go down the wrong path today.

00:10:14.460 --> 00:10:15.180
Out!

00:10:19.890 --> 00:10:22.330
Shigeno lost two points right off the bat.

00:10:22.330 --> 00:10:24.000
It's another bad game...

00:10:27.770 --> 00:10:28.850
Out!

00:10:28.850 --> 00:10:30.480
All right, good.

00:10:30.480 --> 00:10:32.430
You held them at two.

00:10:32.430 --> 00:10:33.790
It's just the beginning.

00:10:33.790 --> 00:10:35.030
Let's change gears.

00:10:35.630 --> 00:10:36.440
Damn it!

00:10:36.960 --> 00:10:39.010
Who does that umpire think he is?

00:10:39.010 --> 00:10:44.090
What's baseball when every strike is a ball?

00:10:44.090 --> 00:10:45.940
Hey, move on.

00:10:47.180 --> 00:10:50.800
That error really cost us, man...

00:10:51.370 --> 00:10:55.470
And it doesn't help that a certain someone has a batting average below .200.

00:10:55.470 --> 00:10:57.010
Guys, that's enough.

00:10:57.010 --> 00:10:58.470
Shut up!

00:11:00.590 --> 00:11:01.630
Play!

00:11:06.310 --> 00:11:08.020
Strike!

00:11:08.390 --> 00:11:09.280
What?

00:11:09.280 --> 00:11:11.790
Hasn't he been calling that a ball?

00:11:11.790 --> 00:11:13.790
Why's it suddenly a strike?

00:11:13.790 --> 00:11:17.640
Is he favoring the Browns?

00:11:17.640 --> 00:11:19.020
Half a ball difference.

00:11:19.020 --> 00:11:19.900
What?

00:11:19.900 --> 00:11:24.870
From what I saw, I'd say Ahn's low, outside pitch was half a ball more inside than yours.

00:11:28.330 --> 00:11:29.190
Strike!

00:11:29.190 --> 00:11:31.220
They each throw a pitch in just about the same place,

00:11:31.220 --> 00:11:34.670
yet a small difference makes one a strike and the other a ball.

00:11:34.670 --> 00:11:38.660
This is going to bring Shigeno down even more.

00:11:38.660 --> 00:11:43.850
Not to mention that our guys won't be able to get any decent hits

00:11:43.850 --> 00:11:45.580
against a bunch of low, outside pitches.

00:11:45.580 --> 00:11:46.560
Out!

00:11:48.700 --> 00:11:49.850
Strike out!

00:11:58.960 --> 00:12:00.070
Out!

00:12:13.210 --> 00:12:13.750
There!

00:12:14.740 --> 00:12:15.630
Ball!

00:12:15.630 --> 00:12:19.260
Shigeno doesn't seem too sharp today.

00:12:19.260 --> 00:12:23.590
On the other hand, the Browns' Ahn is playing it safe.

00:12:24.420 --> 00:12:29.930
The Hornets have gone seven innings without being able to connect an attack.

00:12:29.930 --> 00:12:33.440
Seems like home plate will be impossible to reach in this game.

00:12:35.220 --> 00:12:38.270
I wonder if it's going to be dragged out like this again.

00:12:38.850 --> 00:12:43.260
With the umpire against us, there's no way we can win the game.

00:12:43.260 --> 00:12:44.070
Shigeno!

00:12:44.070 --> 00:12:44.860
What do you want?

00:12:45.360 --> 00:12:48.030
We're changing pitching patterns this inning.

00:12:49.380 --> 00:12:53.000
There's no point in changing the pattern with that guy judging my pitches.

00:12:54.140 --> 00:12:58.130
If you can't trust the judge, then throw them all down the middle.

00:12:59.450 --> 00:13:02.060
I won't move my mitt from the center.

00:13:02.060 --> 00:13:03.590
Wh-What?

00:13:08.560 --> 00:13:09.720
Or are you

00:13:09.720 --> 00:13:12.720
too scared to fight without pitching to the edges?

00:13:15.720 --> 00:13:16.940
Are you kidding me?

00:13:17.420 --> 00:13:19.580
Let's do this!

00:13:19.580 --> 00:13:20.270
All right.

00:13:20.270 --> 00:13:22.240
H-Hey, wait a minute.

00:13:22.680 --> 00:13:24.130
You've got to be kidding.

00:13:24.130 --> 00:13:25.570
Let's be a little more serious here.

00:13:26.200 --> 00:13:28.550
I'm always serious.

00:13:28.550 --> 00:13:31.160
A showdown right through the middle sounds like fun.

00:13:31.530 --> 00:13:33.320
Hey, wait a minute.

00:13:33.320 --> 00:13:36.590
If you do that, they're gonna hit your pitches.

00:13:36.590 --> 00:13:41.130
Then as the fielders, we just have to get them all out.

00:13:44.420 --> 00:13:45.880
Murdoch.

00:13:46.390 --> 00:13:47.800
All of them?

00:13:47.800 --> 00:13:48.920
Are you...

00:13:48.920 --> 00:13:50.080
Yeah.

00:13:51.320 --> 00:13:57.720
Mitchell isn't the only guy keeping Shigeno down today.

00:13:57.720 --> 00:13:59.810
Your defense is just as bad.

00:13:59.810 --> 00:14:01.510
Hey, wait a minute.

00:14:01.510 --> 00:14:04.480
He's the only guy who made an error.

00:14:05.060 --> 00:14:07.850
On record, that is.

00:14:07.850 --> 00:14:09.180
But Robinson,

00:14:10.160 --> 00:14:13.390
when that ball went your way in the first inning,

00:14:13.390 --> 00:14:18.120
you could've got both runners out if you went for the ball instead of waiting.

00:14:18.510 --> 00:14:19.710
And Roy,

00:14:20.610 --> 00:14:23.630
after you covered James' error,

00:14:24.070 --> 00:14:30.800
you were so scared of losing a run that you threw for home instead of holding the runner at second.

00:14:31.690 --> 00:14:34.980
If you had thought about what you were doing then,

00:14:36.280 --> 00:14:40.400
we could have prevented that second run from the sacrifice fly.

00:14:41.210 --> 00:14:45.230
In the recent games, you've all been making stupid plays.

00:14:45.920 --> 00:14:48.420
I know you just don't want to lose,

00:14:48.420 --> 00:14:50.600
but if you keep playing like that, we'll just keep losing.

00:14:53.220 --> 00:14:55.450
That snotty rookie told me...

00:14:56.580 --> 00:15:01.020
something the other day, and I'll say it to you now.

00:15:01.410 --> 00:15:04.920
You're not playing against the umpires or your teammates!

00:15:05.560 --> 00:15:07.610
Shigeno, that goes for you, too!

00:15:07.610 --> 00:15:10.240
You should at least listen to your own words.

00:15:10.240 --> 00:15:11.340
Murdoch...

00:15:18.450 --> 00:15:19.890
What are you standing around for?

00:15:19.890 --> 00:15:20.920
Let's go.

00:15:22.130 --> 00:15:23.840
Y-Yeah.

00:15:25.260 --> 00:15:26.230
H-Hey!

00:15:26.230 --> 00:15:27.790
Where do you think—

00:15:30.940 --> 00:15:33.210
Let's leave this in their hands.

00:15:39.250 --> 00:15:41.160
Murdoch's right.

00:15:41.740 --> 00:15:42.490
Play!

00:15:46.270 --> 00:15:51.050
The strict calls and all this pressure to win distracted me, but...

00:15:54.560 --> 00:15:55.620
Strike!

00:15:57.070 --> 00:16:00.620
Only one player can decide the flow of the game,

00:16:00.620 --> 00:16:02.330
and that's the pitcher!

00:16:08.770 --> 00:16:09.730
Strike!

00:16:12.780 --> 00:16:14.200
Strike out!

00:16:15.410 --> 00:16:17.870
Th-Three pitches?

00:16:19.360 --> 00:16:23.030
Looks like Keene's finally decided to take a stand.

00:16:23.030 --> 00:16:24.990
Hey, what do you mean?

00:16:25.720 --> 00:16:28.040
Just watch and learn.

00:16:31.730 --> 00:16:34.010
Three pitches right down the middle?

00:16:38.560 --> 00:16:40.270
Strike!

00:16:41.940 --> 00:16:44.260
Stop getting cocky, you rookie.

00:16:48.060 --> 00:16:49.440
Don't take me for an idiot!

00:16:52.620 --> 00:16:53.570
Out!

00:16:54.410 --> 00:16:55.450
Nice!

00:16:58.140 --> 00:17:01.410
Now hitting, number 11: Pelfrey!

00:17:02.490 --> 00:17:04.500
I don't know what you're thinking, but...

00:17:05.430 --> 00:17:08.540
I'm not letting you take us down with just fastballs.

00:17:17.250 --> 00:17:18.010
Out!

00:17:18.010 --> 00:17:20.040
Nice play.

00:17:25.390 --> 00:17:27.250
Good going!

00:17:28.400 --> 00:17:31.070
All right, we still have two innings left.

00:17:31.560 --> 00:17:33.900
In any case, we need to get a point first.

00:17:34.380 --> 00:17:35.210
Yeah.

00:17:35.790 --> 00:17:36.700
No.

00:17:36.700 --> 00:17:38.390
Let's end the game this inning.

00:17:39.560 --> 00:17:43.750
That's the mindset we need to achieve our goal.

00:17:44.950 --> 00:17:47.460
Our goal? What's that?

00:17:48.090 --> 00:17:50.380
The title, what else?

00:17:51.940 --> 00:17:53.920
Th-The title?

00:17:54.340 --> 00:17:59.020
With everyone here, we have enough manpower to win the title.

00:17:59.020 --> 00:18:05.540
But if you're not willing to take the chance when you have the ability to, we don't need you!

00:18:06.320 --> 00:18:08.440
Go back to the minors and start over.

00:18:12.920 --> 00:18:16.180
The Hornets aren't a bunch of cowards.

00:18:16.180 --> 00:18:18.200
Yeah, not a single one of us.

00:18:18.200 --> 00:18:20.550
All right, let's do this!

00:18:20.550 --> 00:18:21.240
Who's with me?

00:18:21.240 --> 00:18:22.910
Yeah!

00:18:23.340 --> 00:18:24.250
Okay!

00:18:29.190 --> 00:18:30.170
Let's do this!

00:18:31.700 --> 00:18:33.970
I don't know what you're partying about,

00:18:33.970 --> 00:18:38.110
but with a line-up with just three hits, nothing you do's gonna help you.

00:18:41.040 --> 00:18:42.760
I'll definitely get on base.

00:18:46.720 --> 00:18:47.540
Foul!

00:18:48.890 --> 00:18:49.730
Robinson!

00:18:50.530 --> 00:18:52.670
Calm down and watch the ball!

00:18:56.440 --> 00:18:57.610
Ball!

00:18:57.980 --> 00:19:01.750
Ahn's control's starting to fail.

00:19:01.750 --> 00:19:02.720
Yes.

00:19:02.720 --> 00:19:06.670
That pitch was half a ball outside the strike zone.

00:19:07.280 --> 00:19:08.400
All right!

00:19:08.400 --> 00:19:10.290
Let's go, Robinson!

00:19:11.310 --> 00:19:12.050
Ball!

00:19:12.050 --> 00:19:12.960
Ball four!

00:19:12.960 --> 00:19:14.030
Wh-What?

00:19:14.030 --> 00:19:15.920
Woohoo!

00:19:15.920 --> 00:19:17.270
G-Good.

00:19:17.270 --> 00:19:18.350
Good eye.

00:19:19.010 --> 00:19:20.190
He showed us.

00:19:23.500 --> 00:19:24.800
Ball!

00:19:33.100 --> 00:19:34.890
All right!

00:19:34.890 --> 00:19:36.480
No out and runners on first and third!

00:19:43.240 --> 00:19:44.390
Ball!

00:19:44.390 --> 00:19:45.730
Ball four!

00:19:58.490 --> 00:19:59.990
Out!

00:19:59.990 --> 00:20:00.840
Damn!

00:20:00.840 --> 00:20:03.260
Man, that was close!

00:20:03.990 --> 00:20:05.930
Now hitting, number 1:

00:20:06.560 --> 00:20:09.560
Jeff Keene!

00:20:13.460 --> 00:20:15.030
Hit it big, Keene!

00:20:15.030 --> 00:20:16.600
Finish him!

00:20:16.600 --> 00:20:18.350
You've got this!

00:20:18.350 --> 00:20:20.590
Keene, give us a hit.

00:20:21.570 --> 00:20:22.260
Please.

00:20:23.340 --> 00:20:24.430
End the game.

00:20:47.410 --> 00:20:48.860
Safe! Safe!

00:20:51.270 --> 00:20:52.270
All right!

00:20:52.270 --> 00:20:53.440
We turned it around!

00:21:00.230 --> 00:21:00.940
Yeah!

00:21:00.940 --> 00:21:02.080
This game's over.

00:21:02.080 --> 00:21:03.490
Yeah!

00:21:03.490 --> 00:21:07.550
We're in the top of the ninth and the Browns have two outs and no runners on base.

00:21:07.550 --> 00:21:09.630
The Hornets are just a step away from victory!

00:21:16.080 --> 00:21:17.380
Low and outside?

00:21:26.080 --> 00:21:27.970
That was a strike, wasn't it?

00:21:30.450 --> 00:21:32.140
Strike out!

00:21:32.140 --> 00:21:34.020
Game over!

00:21:34.020 --> 00:21:36.110
All right!

00:21:36.110 --> 00:21:37.710
Shigeno!

00:21:46.720 --> 00:21:47.820
Nice pitch.

00:21:50.170 --> 00:21:52.730
You too, nice call.

00:21:55.710 --> 00:21:56.720
All right!

00:21:56.720 --> 00:21:58.630
We did it!

00:21:59.120 --> 00:22:02.360
Looks like the Hornets finally got some reins.

00:22:19.340 --> 00:22:23.630
Your hip is looking a lot worse than I anticipated.

00:22:24.410 --> 00:22:27.780
I'm not absolutely sure without further inspection,

00:22:28.240 --> 00:22:33.870
but at this rate, you may not be able to pitch to the end of the season.

00:22:46.050 --> 00:22:51.550
kaze to hizashi no naka de

00:22:46.050 --> 00:22:51.550
Amid the wind and the sunlight,

00:22:53.430 --> 00:22:58.270
hashiru anata wo miteta

00:22:53.430 --> 00:22:58.270
I followed you running with my eyes.

00:22:58.480 --> 00:22:59.940
yume wo

00:22:58.480 --> 00:23:03.110
You were chasing your dream.

00:23:00.810 --> 00:23:03.110
oikaketeiru

00:23:03.110 --> 00:23:05.900
ground no ue ni

00:23:03.110 --> 00:23:09.110
Your sweat fell on the baseball field,

00:23:05.900 --> 00:23:09.110
ochiru ase ga

00:23:09.570 --> 00:23:13.080
mabushikatta yo

00:23:09.570 --> 00:23:13.080
and it looked so dazzling.

00:23:13.740 --> 00:23:20.500
wakariatteirutsumori datta

00:23:13.740 --> 00:23:20.500
I thought we understood each other,

00:23:21.120 --> 00:23:27.800
issho ni warai naita kara

00:23:21.120 --> 00:23:27.800
because you and I both shared laughs and tears.

00:23:28.470 --> 00:23:32.550
kokoro no ue ni

00:23:28.470 --> 00:23:35.570
There are identical footprints on both of our hearts.

00:23:32.550 --> 00:23:35.570
onaji ashi ato

00:23:35.570 --> 00:23:38.180
zutto mae kara

00:23:35.570 --> 00:23:43.230
I had unconciously liked you for a long while now.

00:23:38.180 --> 00:23:39.940
kizukazu ni

00:23:39.940 --> 00:23:43.230
suki ni natta

00:23:43.230 --> 00:23:45.520
atsuku sugoshita

00:23:43.230 --> 00:23:50.360
My feelings were hiding in the days we spent, full of passion.

00:23:45.520 --> 00:23:50.360
tsukihi ni kakureteta

00:23:50.360 --> 00:23:52.950
zutto mae kara

00:23:50.360 --> 00:23:58.040
We've been drawn to each other for so long now.

00:23:52.950 --> 00:23:54.830
otagai ni

00:23:54.830 --> 00:23:58.040
hikareteita

00:23:58.040 --> 00:24:00.250
kono kimochi wa

00:23:58.040 --> 00:24:07.250
This feeling I have for you is what youth left behind.

00:24:00.250 --> 00:24:07.250
seishun no wasuremono

00:24:09.960 --> 00:24:15.380
Preview

00:24:09.960 --> 00:24:15.380
Preview

00:24:10.590 --> 00:24:13.380
What? You want me on a commercial?

00:24:13.380 --> 00:24:14.720
Are you kidding me?

00:24:14.720 --> 00:24:17.510
And now there's some weird woman chasing me around.

00:24:18.100 --> 00:24:21.700
I'm definitely not doing it!

00:24:21.700 --> 00:24:25.020
Next time, on Major: An Uninvited Guest.

00:24:25.020 --> 00:24:27.380
Run toward the stage of your dreams!

00:24:25.020 --> 00:24:30.700
Next Time

00:24:25.020 --> 00:24:30.700
Next Time

00:24:25.020 --> 00:24:30.700
An Uninvited Guest

00:24:25.020 --> 00:24:30.700
An Uninvited Guest
